  "rules": [
    "Model consistently underestimates volatility and fails to capture sudden price spikes (e.g., Example 4 & 5 where true outcomes reach ~60 while forecasts cap near 52).",
    "Forecasts exhibit a strong downward bias in the first 10 days, often predicting declines that are immediately reversed by sharp rallies.",
    "Sentiment history shows no predictive power; model errors occur regardless of sentiment spikes (e.g., positive sentiment at day 6 did not prevent forecast failure).",
    "Model assumes mean reversion to a lower baseline (~52) rather than following the actual trend or range expansion observed in true outcomes.",
    "Horizon-specific error: Model is overly conservative on short-term horizons (<10 days) and completely misses long-term upside potential (>15 days).",
    "Correction heuristic: Apply an upward volatility adjustment factor of +3% to +5% to the forecasted path, especially when recent history shows a range > 6 points."
  ]
}
